 ## Background
-Originating from work on generalizing splatting with decaying anisotropic radial basis functions, these techniques were introduced to improve the fidelity of Gaussian splatting rendering [S1]. The stabilization approach addresses the common issue of "sparkles" or aliasing in novel view synthesis, while the correction methods address the geometric mismatch between the projected Gaussian and the true integrated density.
+The techniques originate from work on generalizing splatting with decaying anisotropic radial basis functions [S1]. The correction methods were introduced to approximate the relationship between projected 2D covariances and actual 2D covariances, replacing complex MLPs or Simpson's rule integration with linear regression or scalar factors [S1]. The stabilization approach addresses aliasing in novel view synthesis, while correction methods address the geometric mismatch between the projected Gaussian and the true integrated density [S1].
